          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em May spectral sequence
            (
            %a{:href => "#May64"}> May 64
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#May74"} May 74
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Ravenel86"} Ravenel 86, 3.2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
            that computes the second page of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+Adams+spectral+sequence"} classical Adams spectral sequence
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ext"} Ext
            = succeed "-groups," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cotor"} Cotor
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "cotensor+product#ComoduleHomInTermsOfCotensorProduct"} this lemma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comodules"} comodules
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebras"} commutative Hopf algebras
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+Steenrod+algebra"} dual Steenrod algebra
            in the classical case) starting from the corresponding
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ext
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+graded"} associated graded
            Hopf algebra.
          %p
            The May spectral sequence is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+complex"} spectral sequence of a filtered complex
            induced by suitably filtering the canonical (but intractable)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+complex"} bar complex
            model for
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ext"} Ext
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cotor"} Cotor
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Ravenel86"} Ravenel 86, chapter 3, section 2
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Kochman96"} Kochman 96, section 5.3
