                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes A \to A\otimes \Gamma
              and hence the right vertical morphisms exists by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of cokernels. This is the compatible left module structure on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\Gamma}
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              For the second statement, consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
